Package: ergMargins
Type: Package
Title: Process Analysis for Exponential Random Graph Models
Version: 1.6.2.9001
Authors@R: c(person("Scott", "Duxbury", email = "duxbury@email.unc.edu", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Ben", "Rosche", email = "benjamin.rosche@gmail.com", role = c("ctb", "cre")))
Maintainer: Ben Rosche <benjamin.rosche@gmail.com>
Description: Unofficial fork of 'ergMargins' 1.6.2 by Scott Duxbury, in which marginal
    effects respect the model's sample-space constraints, such as blockdiag(),
    and the layers of multilayer models fitted with 'ergm.multi'.
    Calculates marginal effects and conducts process analysis in exponential family random graph models (ERGM).
    Includes functions to conduct mediation and moderation analyses and to diagnose
    multicollinearity.
    Duxbury, Scott W (2021) <doi:10.1177/0049124120986178>.
    Long, J. Scott, and Sarah Mustillo (2018) <doi:10.1177/0049124118799374>.
    Mize, Trenton D. (2019) <doi:10.15195/v6.a4>.
    Karlson, Kristian Bernt, Anders Holm, and Richard Breen (2012) <doi:10.1177/0081175012444861>.
    Duxbury, Scott W (2018) <doi:10.1177/0049124118782543>.
    Duxbury, Scott W, Jenna Wertsching (2023) <doi:10.1016/j.socnet.2023.02.003>.
    Huang, Peng, Carter Butts (2023) <doi:10.1016/j.socnet.2023.07.001>.
URL: https://github.com/benrosche/ergMargins/tree/constraints, https://github.com/sduxbury/ergMargins
BugReports: https://github.com/benrosche/ergMargins/issues
